<title>USA: ConEd sees Indian Pt nuke on line this wknd.</title>
<headline>ConEd sees Indian Pt nuke on line this wknd.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Consolidated Edison of New York (ConEd) said Wednesday its 975 megawatt (MW) Indian Point 2 nuclear unit will likely begin contributing to the electricity grid this weekend.</p>
<p>&quot;We expect we'll start heating up Friday, and we'll hit the grid late this weekend,&quot; company spokesman Michael Spall said.</p>
<p>The unit's restart was delayed when operators moved it from hot to cold shutdown late last week for valve repairs.</p>
<p>Indian Point 2 was originally shut Jan 27 to repair a feedwater valve.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
